# VietCaPhe blog posts

Read `docs/blog/PLAYBOOK.md` before writing. Pick ideas from `docs/blog/IDEAS.md` and update it after publishing.

## Non-negotiables (public content)
- VietCaPhe sells **green, unroasted beans to roasters only**. Never imply we sell roasted coffee or supply cafés.
- Never mention: the mill name or site, lot codes (GC…), trade names (Eco-premium, Honey SMOOTH, "Clean" lines), screen size, Highland Essence, VND/dong, or any VietCaPhe price.
- Public benchmark prices (e.g. ICE robusta futures, ICO indicator) are fine with a dated, linked source.
- Never invent customers, quotes, case studies or statistics. Case studies need real details from Erik.
- Never name or quote customer reviewers.
- Australian English, plain language, sentence-case headings, no em dashes.

## Every post
1. File: `src/content/blog/<keyword-slug>.mdx`, copied from `docs/blog/post-template.mdx`. The slug is the URL.
2. Frontmatter passes the schema in `src/content.config.ts` (title ≤ 80, `seoTitle` ≤ 60 if needed, description 80–160, 3–6 takeaways, 3–6 FAQ, every factual claim's source in `sources`).
3. H2s are the questions roasters actually ask. Each H2 opens with `<Answer>`: 40–60 words that make sense quoted alone.
4. At least one bespoke interactive or animated graphic in `src/components/blog/`, used inside `<Figure label caption>` with `client:visible`. Reuse existing graphics where they fit.
5. A comparison table or checklist wherever the topic allows.
6. 3+ internal links (other posts, `/#coffee`, `/#process`, `/#contact`) and a closing sample CTA.
7. `npm run build`, then check desktop + mobile in the browser, and `dist/og/<slug>.png`.
8. Update `docs/blog/IDEAS.md` (move the idea to Published, add new ideas found while researching) and link to the new post from 1–2 older posts.
